40,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The timing shows a full pass takes over an hour and a half. Also, an outside firm requires us to tidy up before they arrive, meaning we wouldn't be completely free from the work.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the data suggests a certain imbalance. The kitchen workload is driven by a small minority, and our calendar reveals that some of us are practically guests in our own home for weeks at a time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found out why the rooms are so weird! Some people think ""done"" means just wiping the sink, while others do the whole floor! No wonder it's a mystery every time I walk in!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that we have quite a few extra bottles of spray, and we're spending about 2,300 yen a month. Also, the management office charges 4,200 yen an hour for a cleaner.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The previous tenants left a warning that rigid divisions can lead to silence between friends. Also, the bathroom grout returns to its state quickly due to poor ventilation, regardless of the effort spent.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, if some people are rarely home, it's unfair for them to do the same amount of work, but it's also unfair for those of us who are here to carry the load.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Minako. It is a curious paradox where the absent are spared the mess but the present are burdened by it, all while the ""contribution"" remains nominally equal on paper. Logic suggests we adjust for actual usage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako @Benjamin, that sounds like a puzzle! But wait, the chat logs show we fight because people forget things. If we just change who does what, will we still be arguing about who forgot the sink?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying that we are fighting over such small things. Perhaps if we have a clear, gentle way to remind each other, we can avoid those disagreements and keep our hearts light.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance, is it not? When we focus only on the logic of usage or the precision of a checklist, we risk forgetting that we are companions first and cleaners second. Let us be mindful of the spirit.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Sakura, a clear definition of ""done"" would solve the arguments. However, we can't ignore that the total time is significant. If we hire a firm, we still have to tidy up, which adds more time to our schedule.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, indeed. If we are merely tidying for a professional, we've simply traded scrubbing for organizing. I suspect a system that acknowledges the disparity in usage would be far more sustainable than a flat fee or a rigid rotation.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"But if we just adjust for usage, will the rooms still be a surprise? I want to know for sure that the floor is clean before I go in! Maybe we need a super-clear checklist so everyone knows exactly what ""done"" means!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"A checklist sounds like a wonderful idea, Sakura. It would be so kind of us to help each other by being clear about what needs doing, so no one feels overwhelmed or confused.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A checklist can provide clarity, but we must be careful not to turn our home into a workplace. If we become too focused on the rules, we may lose the warmth that makes this house a home.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We need to be realistic. Whether we use a checklist or a professional, the time commitment is still there. We should consider how to distribute these hours so no one person is overwhelmed by the workload.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A realistic distribution is the only way to avoid resentment. If we ignore the fact that some of us are rarely here while others are constant kitchen residents, we are simply designing a system destined to fail.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I agree! But let's make sure the ""realistic"" part includes a way to stop the guessing game! If we have a checklist and a fair way to share the work, the house will be sparkly and we'll all be happy!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. While we decide on the work, I hope we can also find a simple way to handle the costs of our supplies, so no one feels burdened by paying for everything.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such a thoughtful exchange. Let us remember that the most beautiful homes are not those with the cleanest floors, but those where the inhabitants feel seen and valued. I look forward to our options.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
