65,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A is too rigid and doesn't account for the time burden. Option B still requires tidying, and Option C could lead to burnout if one person is stuck with the kitchen.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a recipe for resentment, as it ignores the usage disparities I discovered. Option B is a financial drain for a partial solution, and Option C risks creating a permanent underclass of scrubbers.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option B sounds like magic because a pro does it! But if we still have to tidy up, it's not a total mystery-solver. Option A is like a game, but what if the ""done"" rules are still confusing?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B would be very helpful for our tired shoulders, but I worry about the cost. If we choose it, we must be very careful and clear about how we settle the bills each month.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option C reminds me of the warning from the previous tenants; permanent divisions can build walls of silence between us. We must choose a path that preserves our friendship above all else.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, if we want to avoid a ""permanent underclass,"" Option C is indeed risky. However, Option A's rigidity means the workload hits all at once, which is exactly what I want to avoid. We need a balance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, a balance is ideal, but Option A is the antithesis of balance; it treats a ghost-tenant and a gourmet chef as equals. If we must choose from these, we need the one least likely to spark a revolution.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Benjamin, a revolution sounds scary! But wait, if we do Option A, can we add my super-clear checklist to it? That way, no matter whose turn it is, the room is always sparkly and not a surprise!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"That would be a lovely addition, Sakura. A checklist would be so helpful for everyone. I just hope that whichever option we pick, we can also agree on a fair way to share the cost of the sponges and sprays.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Sakura, your spirit is wonderful. A checklist can be a bridge of understanding. However, let us consider that the most sustainable system is one where no one feels they are carrying a burden in silence. Kindness is the best detergent.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Sakura, a checklist helps with quality, but it doesn't reduce the hours. Option B is the most consistent, even with the tidying, because it removes the heavy scrubbing from our daily lives. It's the most stable choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, stability is a virtue, but paying for a service that requires us to do the preparatory work is a rather expensive way to achieve a partial result. It's a bit like paying a chef to cook but still having to chop all the vegetables.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, but if we pay for a pro, will they use a checklist too? I just want to stop guessing if the bathroom is scary or not! If Option A has a checklist, it's like a treasure map to a clean house!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I think Sakura's treasure map is a wonderful idea. If we choose Option A, we can all help each other follow the list. It would be so gentle on our wallets, too, leaving us more for treats!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Shizue, your focus on our shared joy is a blessing. While Option A may seem simple, we must ensure it does not become a source of hidden tension. Let us choose the path that keeps our hearts open.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Minako,,"Considering the time it actually takes to clean, Option A is the most fair in terms of labor distribution, provided we use Sakura's checklist. Option B is too expensive for what it offers. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we are limited to these three choices, Option A is the least offensive. While it is logically flawed regarding usage, it is far more sustainable than a financial drain or permanent servitude. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm voting for A too! As long as we have my super-clear checklist, the mystery is solved and the house will be sparkly for everyone! Yay! I vote for A!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. Option A is a very kind way to share the work, and with Sakura's lovely checklist, we can all support one another. I vote for A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see such a consensus born from mutual respect. While no system is perfect, the spirit of cooperation you have shown is the true cleaning agent for our home. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
